  "notes": "The State Secretariat describes the surviving main building’s front and rear verandas, broad glazed side screens, teak and iron structure and blend of tropical West Javanese and European architecture. The Rijksmuseum’s c.1844–46 study depicts the raised front and historical roof profile. The estate guide describes 11 approach steps and the provincial government records a floor raise of about two meters."
